[32;1m[1;3mThought: I need to identify the mathematical structure: decision variables are (a) binary plant-opening decisions (whether to build each plant), and (b) continuous shipment quantities from each plant to each customer. The objective is to minimize total cost = sum of fixed opening costs (for opened plants) + sum of per-unit transportation costs (for all shipments). Constraints: (1) each customer's demand must be fully satisfied; (2) total shipments from each plant cannot exceed its capacity (if opened); (3) shipments from a plant to a customer are only allowed if the plant is opened. The key coupling is between facility-opening (fixed cost) and assignment/shipment decisions. This is the classic capacitated facility location structure.

Action: FileQA

Action Input: binary plant-opening decisions with fixed opening costs, plant capacities, continuous shipment quantities from plants to customers, per-unit transport costs, customer demand satisfaction, plant capacity constraints, and coupling between opening and shipment decisions
